Z||000000||mikabika||09-06-2001||07:19 AM||||I'm thinking of changing out my steering stabilizer shock on my 87 GT. Is this a simple task, or do I need 3 guys, and a horse to do it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TONY_C||09-06-2001||08:00 AM||||It's as easy as changing a shock on the wheel, probably even easier.||||reg||1
Z||000002||roadwarrior||09-06-2001||09:30 AM||||it involves undoing two bolts, taking off the old stabalizer, re-instaling the new one and tightening up the two bolts, can it get much easier?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||09-06-2001||10:01 AM||||The bolts even came out easily on my father's 87 coupe, despite 13 years of rust and corrosion from road salt on them!  Its really easy!  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||09-06-2001||10:36 AM||||I dont think there worth any effort, all they do is soften the shock of hitting small bumps and transferring to to steering wheel. I dont have one, its just something almost usless that can break. My Mercedes SL had one too, I took it off and never noticed any difference, except the rattle stopped.||||reg||1
